Kintsugi is an opinionated fork of AgentsInTheCloud by Lucas Meijer.
Original source: https://github.com/lucasmeijer/AgentsInTheCloud
License: MIT (see LICENSE). Original copyright retained.

The Docker runtime is pinned to an upstream AgentsInTheCloud image.

Kintsugi includes portions adapted from @earendil-works/gondolin.

Source: https://github.com/earendil-works/gondolin
License: Apache License 2.0

Adapted components include HTTP secret placeholder substitution, host pattern matching,
and internal IP detection helpers.

Kintsugi's Codex-compatible subagent tool descriptions and message envelopes are adapted
from OpenAI Codex (https://github.com/openai/codex), commit
574a36ff99f0807a24f5b043f593122bf151908d, licensed under Apache License 2.0.
Copyright OpenAI. The license is included in docs/licenses/codex-LICENSE.

The Draw.io Work view uses the embed protocol approach of Rui Carmo's piclaw-addons
(drawio-editor), MIT licensed, and bundles draw.io v31.4.2, Apache-2.0 licensed.
Source: https://github.com/rcarmo/piclaw-addons and https://github.com/jgraph/drawio
Licenses and vendor provenance are included in packages/drawio/vendor/.

Selected UI/syntax/ANSI palettes are adapted from PiClaw by Rui Carmo:
https://github.com/rcarmo/piclaw/tree/34516cabd8e56f61bd1b7150e0c87c244694533e
(runtime/src/core/ui-theme-catalogue.ts and runtime/web/src/ui/theme-palette.ts).
Includes Catppuccin Mocha, Monokai Pro, Dracula, Gruvbox, Noctis, Lumon, AS/400,
SynthWave ’84 and Petrol & Copper (named Fallout in Kintsugi).
UI/ANSI contrast adjustments are baked into CSS; no PiClaw runtime is loaded.

